message="CHROMIUM: drm/img-rogue/mt8173: Refactor power callbacks  Move the IMG integration wrapper callbacks to sysconfig.c.  This allows us to remove saving a global copy of the platform_device in mfgsys.c.  Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47249 TEST=build &amp; sanity test webgl on oak-rev4  Change-Id: I723ab017163a16607cc3fc34eccb0a74359b92e7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/311924 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Frank Binns &lt;frank.binns@imgtec.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="311924" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/24/311924/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0f2a4b231ebbae59c729110b0e4e5519df044623" commit="6880ac9b3ae8591b63ba74f5bc2644c9df577559" commit_message="bundle_firmware: In RW-CBFS mode, add ecrw and pdrw if available  They won't be in their own fmap regions anymore (with the hash somewhere else), but both will be in CBFS, with their precalculated hashes in the CBFS file header.  BUG=chromium:445938 TEST=with all the MULTIPLE_CBFS_INSTANCES stuff enabled, FW_MAIN_[AB] contain ecrw and pdrw, depending on the hardware in question, both with a SHA256 hash.  Change-Id: I0f2a4b231ebbae59c729110b0e4e5519df044623 Signed-off-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/306590 Commit-Ready: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="306590" owner_email="pgeorgi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/dev-util" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/dev-util" ref="refs/changes/90/306590/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I200dd4822bb57772c992d051a760d6b02472c594" commit="cc7dcaff6bf469f819eaf458102104c59067705e" commit_message="Send finalize request to shopfloor after in-place wipe  Originally we send finalize request to shopfloor just before wiping. However, if wiping failed, data in shopfloor still indicates the dut is finalized.  For in-place wipe, we can inform shopfloor after successfully wiping.  BUG=chromium:544021 TEST=Test in-place wipe on Paine  Change-Id: I200dd4822bb57772c992d051a760d6b02472c594 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/311903 Commit-Ready: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shun-Hsing Ou &lt;shunhsingou@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bowgo Tsai &lt;bowgotsai@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="311903" owner_email="shunhsingou@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/03/311903/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I26396af1fed4e6f4f8c47c3cef45488947225614" commit="8cda3ebacb3bf55901894a029fc7e7de3b675c65" commit_message="gooftool: Probe both SOC and HDA drivers on x86 platforms.  Recent x86 CPU may be released as SOC and start using SOC drivers, which makes platform-specific probing rules (arm=SOC, x86=PCI/HDA) failed.  To support both we should merge all probing approaches again.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47478 TEST=gooftool probe # found ASOC and HDA.  Change-Id: I26396af1fed4e6f4f8c47c3cef45488947225614 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/311902 Commit-Ready: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hsu Wei-Cheng &lt;mojahsu@chromiu